$\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\iint_D2\\,dA=2\\operatorname{area}(D)=2\\pi.$$" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702642 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702642 1083 #uuid "ba61bd9f-1b0e-581b-ac75-c6723448df83" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702643 1058 #edb/ref 17592186702548 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702643 1062 #uuid "be730a14-e931-593b-901c-9c7b5c62149a" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702643 1063 #edb/ref 17592186702644 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702644 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049159 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702644 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049606 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702644 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049875 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702644 1089 #edb/ref 17592186702540 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702644 1090 #uuid "c202c33f-a416-5624-b491-83e8eb582c42" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702645 1068 #edb/ref 17592186702588 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702645 1071 "**(c)(i)** For $\\mathbf F=\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}},\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}\\right\\rangle$, find its domain.\n\nDomain: {{answer}}." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702645 1072 #uuid "c22bbe58-4929-5199-bc86-6f6e6f712841" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702645 1074 "The denominator vanishes exactly at $(0,0)$. Exclude the origin; the field is smooth everywhere else." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702646 1080 "No. Each generating vector satisfies $z=-2x$, so every linear combination also satisfies $z=-2x$. The target has $x=1$ and $z=-1$, which fails that relation. It is outside the span, so no such linear combination exists." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702646 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702646 1083 #uuid "c2e1fa68-9010-5f23-9d15-43d096747c65" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702647 1080 "The printed $\\psi_t$ is a typo: the denominator must be $\\psi_y$. With $y=y(x)$, differentiate $\\psi(x,y(x))=c$:\n\n$$\\psi_x+\\psi_y\\frac{dy}{dx}=0.$$\n\nWhere $\\psi_y\\ne0$,\n\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{\\psi_x}{\\psi_y}.$$" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702647 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702647 1083 #uuid "c34c8a72-6aec-5e68-bb83-22afb24b29ca" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702648 1058 #edb/ref 17592186702542 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702648 1062 #uuid "c3d25726-9f3e-54ea-8161-1c35367ba1a1" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702648 1063 #edb/ref 17592186702670 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702649 1080 "\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\{(0,0)\\}" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702649 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702649 1083 #uuid "c446cbe1-2870-520a-88fa-d8558d9032bc" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702650 1075 #edb/ref 17592186702560 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702650 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702650 1077 "answer" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702650 1078 #edb/ref 17592186702560 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702650 1079 #uuid "c479ba4b-591e-5cb9-a0e1-516fc2d62542" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702651 1075 #edb/ref 17592186702541 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702651 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702651 1077 "answer" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702651 1078 #edb/ref 17592186702541 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702651 1079 #uuid "c5aecf12-592a-520d-8c44-f9e640f5c8e2" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702652 1075 #edb/ref 17592186702549 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702652 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702652 1077 "answer" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702652 1078 #edb/ref 17592186702549 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702652 1079 #uuid "c63fc8f9-d20a-545b-87bd-ad71e9a55a57" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186702515 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702653 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702653 1077 "answer" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702653 1078 #edb/ref 17592186702515 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702653 1079 #uuid "c88b6705-f18d-5640-b40e-bc841c62e4d8" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702654 1058 #edb/ref 17592186702601 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702654 1062 #uuid "cae52c22-9dbd-5f0f-95a4-01104d05e3cc" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702654 1063 #edb/ref 17592186702563 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702655 1075 #edb/ref 17592186702590 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702655 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702655 1077 "answer" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702655 1078 #edb/ref 17592186702590 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702655 1079 #uuid "cbbef084-1b60-5586-a0c5-aeba84ea1799" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702656 1068 #edb/ref 17592186702630 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702656 1071 "**(c)(iii)** For $\\mathbf F=\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}},\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}\\right\\rangle$, calculate $\\oint_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds$ “using” Green's theorem. Address any failure of its hypotheses." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702656 1072 #uuid "d13cb879-cfc1-5508-95b7-b45cbb676eab" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702656 1074 "For a radius-$\\varepsilon$ circle, the counterclockwise circulation (Problem 2) or outward-from-the-small-disk flux (Problem 3) is $2\\pi\\varepsilon$, which tends to zero. The annulus formula is outer integral minus that inner integral $=2\\pi(1-\\varepsilon)$. The Jacobian factor $r$ cancels the singular factor $1/r$ in the improper area integral." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702657 1080 "They are dependent because $\\vec v_4=-6\\vec v_1+4\\vec v_2+3\\vec v_3$. An independent set with the same span is $\\{\\vec v_1,\\vec v_2,\\vec v_3\\}$." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702657 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702657 1083 #uuid "d2c166ff-5c16-531f-9839-59410b5343f6" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702658 1068 #edb/ref 17592186702583 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702658 1071 "Source exercise: 3.1.3(b) only, printed page 126 (PDF page 138).\n\nFind the determinant of $\\begin{bmatrix}4&3&2\\\\1&7&8\\\\3&-9&3\\end{bmatrix}$ **by hand, without technology**. Show your calculation.\n\nDeterminant: {{answer}}." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702658 1072 #uuid "d33be294-ddfc-53f2-a3fd-b598d37f5af2" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702658 1074 "Expand along the first row, using signs $+,-,+$:\n\n$$4\\begin{vmatrix}7&8\\\\-9&3\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}1&8\\\\3&3\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1&7\\\\3&-9\\end{vmatrix}\n=4(21+72)-3(3-24)+2(-9-21)=372+63-60=375.$$\n\nThe negative cofactor sign on the middle term is essential. A separate elimination check gives the same determinant." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702659 1062 #uuid "d3680e4d-a83e-59c1-98f6-48c84f2ca0ab" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702659 1063 #edb/ref 17592186702677 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702660 1080 "For $r>0$, $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=1/r$. The formal area integral can be interpreted as an improper integral:\n\n$$\\lim_{\\varepsilon\\to0^+}\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\int_\\varepsilon^1\\frac1r\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta\n=\\lim_{\\varepsilon\\to0^+}2\\pi(1-\\varepsilon)=2\\pi.$$\n\nThe standard full-disk theorem does not apply directly because the field is undefined at the origin. The equality can be justified by applying Green's theorem to annuli and taking a limit." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702660 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702660 1083 #uuid "d41b273d-8e09-5af7-a5ea-44d7947cab94" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702661 1075 #edb/ref 17592186702596 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702661 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702661 1077 "answer" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702661 1078 #edb/ref 17592186702596 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702661 1079 #uuid "d4a99cdb-9cdc-5d48-a517-a369789cb6ee" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702662 1080 "\\mathbb R^2\\setminus\\{(0,0)\\}" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702662 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702662 1083 #uuid "d4da990c-4d12-5400-b3ac-10e29ac73afa" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702531 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702548 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702550 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702551 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702566 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702591 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702601 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702608 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702632 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702643 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043 #edb/ref 17592186702654 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702663 1043