 unit circle, parametrize by $\\mathbf r(t)=(\\cos t,\\sin t)$, $0\\le t\\le2\\pi$. The outward unit normal is $(\\cos t,\\sin t)$ and $ds=dt$. Each field in this problem restricts to $(\\cos t,\\sin t)$ on $C$, so the flux is $\\int_0^{2\\pi}(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t)\\,dt=2\\pi$. Equivalently, rotate the field as in Problem 1(c) and use the corresponding circulation in Problem 2." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702676 1084 #edb/ref 17592186702508 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702676 1084 #edb/ref 17592186702543 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702676 1084 #edb/ref 17592186702669 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702676 1085 "Source: Problem 5(a–c), PDF page 6.\n\n**Stream functions produce streamlines.** Let $\\mathbf F=\\langle f,g\\rangle$ be source-free and let $\\psi$ be its stream function, meaning\n\n$$\\psi_y=f,\\qquad\\psi_x=-g.$$\n\nLet $P=(x,y)$ lie on the level curve $\\psi(x,y)=c$. Think of the level curve locally as $y=y(x)$. The source's dependency diagram shows $\\psi$ depending on both $x$ and $y$, with $y$ itself depending on $x$; thus the composite is $\\psi(x,y(x))$." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702676 1086 #uuid "df893de7-f13c-5602-9b56-5e571d7a8b23" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702676 1087 #edb/ref 17592186702669 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702677 1068 #edb/ref 17592186702474 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702677 1071 "**(c)** Find the determinant of $\\begin{bmatrix}4&3\\\\6&2\\end{bmatrix}$ **by hand, without technology**. Show your calculation.\n\nDeterminant: {{answer}}." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702677 1072 #uuid "dfbb5de7-beaf-5fb0-90e3-2d39d8ba3cff" 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702677 1074 "$4(2)-3(6)=8-18=-10$. For a $2\\times2$ matrix, $\\det\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}=ad-bc$. Apply the subtraction in that order." 13194139540774 17592186502323 true] [17592186702678 1088 #edb/ref 